   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Use the power rule. If you raise a non-zero base to an exponent <i>n</i>, and raise that to another exponent, <i>m</i>, you get the base raised to the product of the exponents, which is <span data-math=\"{\\left( {{a^n}} \\right)^m} = {a^{\\left( {n \\times m} \\right)}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\left( {{{11}^4}} \\right)^{12}} = {11^{\\left( {4 \\times 12} \\right)}} = {11^{48}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{11^{48}}\">{11^{48}}</span>"
    }
   ],
